@startuml merged-pr-disposition
title Merged-PR disposition — close vs archive-and-close

skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant "ExecutionController" as Ctrl
participant "CommandBus" as Bus
participant "CloseMergedPullRequestHandler" as Handler
participant "RunDispositionService" as Dispo
participant "WorkItemHsmService" as Hsm
participant "HsmActionHandlers" as Actions
participant "GitHubService" as Gh
participant "GitHubBatchCache" as Cache
participant "WorkItemsService" as Items
participant "GraphWriterService" as Writer
participant "RunStore" as Store
participant "ExecutionService" as Exec
queue "SSE /api/execution/stream" as Sse

== POST /close-merged ==
User -> Ctrl : POST /api/execution/close-merged\n{ work_item_id }
Ctrl -> Bus : execute(CloseMergedPullRequestCommand)
Bus -> Handler : execute(cmd)
Handler -> Dispo : closeMergedPullRequest(id)

Dispo -> Dispo : assertNoActiveRunForWorkItem\n(refuses if any queued/preparing/\ndisambiguating/running)

Dispo -> Hsm : dispatch(user.finalize)

== HSM dispatch (synchronous action handler) ==
Hsm -> Hsm : select transition\nmerged_pr --> done [user.finalize]\naction = closeGhIssue
Hsm -> Actions : closeGhIssue(workItem, event, ctx)
Actions -> Gh : closeIssue(repo, issue_number)
Gh --> Actions : GitHubIssueDetails
Actions -> Actions : ctx.handler_data.closed_issue = {...}
Actions --> Hsm : resolved

Hsm -> Writer : apply([update_work_item\nstate = done, meta = ...])
Hsm -> Hsm : emit work_item_state_changed
Hsm --> Dispo : DispatchResult\n(handler_data includes closed_issue)

== Finalize + dispose runs ==
Dispo -> Items : get(id)
Dispo -> Cache : upsertIssue(repo,\n{ state: closed, ... })
Dispo -> Store : disposeRunsForWorkItem(id, now)
note right of Store
  Walk recentRuns back-to-front,
  splice matching, stamp
  disposed_at on runs/<id>/
  status.json (ENOENT tolerated),
  then scan disk for runs not in
  the buffer and stamp those too.
end note
Store --> Sse : execution_result\n(per disposed run)

Dispo -> Exec : getPreview(repo) (via forwardRef)
Dispo --> Handler : CloseMergedPullRequestResult\n{ work_item, closed_issue,\nremoved_run_ids, dispatch_preview }
Handler --> Bus : result
Bus --> Ctrl
Ctrl --> User : 200

== archive-and-close variant ==
note over Dispo
  POST /archive-and-close-merged runs the same
  flow, but dispatches user.archive_and_finalize.
  The matching transition runs TWO actions:
    1. closeGhIssue
    2. runArchiver → RunDispositionService
       .archiveRunArtifactsAction, which:
       - captureRunSnapshotForWorkItem (merge
         recentRuns + disk scan)
       - movePlanDirToArchives (renameSync
         plans/<slug>/ → archives/<slug>/)
       - archiveRunArtifactsForWorkItem (move
         terminal runs into archives/<slug>/runs/
         and write README.md)
       - stamps ctx.meta.studio_archive +
         ctx.patch_overrides.archive_path
  Result envelope adds an archive block.
end note

@enduml
